    "examples": [
      {
        "question_text": "Use prime factors to decide whether each fraction gives a terminating or a recurring decimal.\n(a) $\\frac{37}{80}$\n(b) $\\frac{23}{28}$",
        "solution_text": "(a) $\\frac{37}{80}$ is in simplest form.\n$80 = 2 \\times 2 \\times 2 \\times 2 \\times 5$.\nOnly the primes $2$ and $5$ appear, so the decimal **terminates**.\n(b) $\\frac{23}{28}$ is in simplest form.\n$28 = 2 \\times 2 \\times 7$.\nThe prime $7$ appears, so the decimal **recurs**."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "Simplify first, then decide whether each fraction gives a terminating or a recurring decimal.\n(a) $\\frac{33}{60}$\n(b) $\\frac{34}{51}$",
        "solution_text": "(a) $\\frac{33}{60} = \\frac{11}{20}$.\n$20 = 2 \\times 2 \\times 5$.\nOnly the primes $2$ and $5$ remain, so the decimal **terminates**.\n(b) $\\frac{34}{51} = \\frac{2}{3}$.\nThe simplified denominator is the prime $3$, so the decimal **recurs**."
      }
    ],
